          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## How to use this graph\n\nStart with the four open questions. Decisions should update the central approach, then constrain the three next steps. Evidence records what Twilite has already taught us; assumptions and risks mark what still needs proof.\n\nThe graph standard should remain small enough to explain, strict enough to compose, and executable enough for validators and agents to repair.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "graph-standardization-idea"
        },
        "visibilityRole": "browser"
      }
    },
